            "target_entity_instance": "Dry",
            "target_entity_type": "ClimateZone",
            "paragraph": "The Brazilian Semiarid is characterized by average annual rainfall equal to or less than 800 mm, Thornthwaite acidity index equal to or less than 0.50, and daily percentage of water deficit equal to or greater than 60% (BRASIL 2017). The Brazilian Semiarid accounts for 18% of the national territory and has an estimated population of 27 870 241 people, representing the most densely populated dryland region in the world (Alval\u00e1 et al. 2017; SUDENE 2018).",
